        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "1. Department Heads are responsible for determining, through direct observation, whether an employee is capable of performing his/her assigned duties. Symptoms of being under the influence of alcohol and drugs include incoherent or belligerent speech, smell of alcohol, difficulty working, or erratic or unusual behavior uncommon to the employee will constitute reasonable suspicion.",
            "block_bbox": [
